Ridge: six observations; two predictors; 1000 independent draws per chain; two chains; seed 8
Horseshoe: five observations; one predictor; 1000 burn-in and 3000 retained draws per chain; four chains; seed 811
Spike-slab: same five observations; 1000 burn-in and 3000 retained draws per chain; four chains; seed 810
Variance-prior: IG(1.5,1.5); native scale priors documented in FitGaussian
Target-tolerance: max(0.01,6*MCSE); MCSE from 100-draw batches
Trace-display: first 300 retained draws per chain; autocorrelation uses all 3000
Evidence-scope: fixed posterior checks and illustrations, not a repeated-dataset study
